tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as a peasant. Your aim is to be the play out all your cards before the landlord does, OR help your teammate (the other peasant) play out their cards before the landlord does. If the landlord plays out all cards first, you lose.\nYou are a Peasant. The Next Player (Right) is the Landlord (ENEMY). The Previous Player (Left) is your TEAMMATE (Peasant). You must cooperate with your teammate to beat the Landlord. The objective is to empty your hand before the landlord does, or help your teammate empty their hand before the landlord does.\n\nYour Hand: ♠3 ♣3 ♣4 ♦4 ♦7 ♠9 ♦9 ♣10 ♠Q ♥Q ♠K ♥2 BlackJoker\nLast Play to Beat: ♠A\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 5 (You): Pass\nTurn 6 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 6 (Prev Player): ♥A ♦A\nTurn 6 (You): Pass\nTurn 7 (Next Player): ♠2 ♦2\nTurn 7 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 7 (You): Pass\nTurn 8 (Next Player): ♠5\nTurn 8 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 8 (You): ♠7\nTurn 9 (Next Player): ♦8\nTurn 9 (Prev Player): ♠10\nTurn 9 (You): ♣K\nTurn 10 (Next Player): ♠A\nTurn 10 (Prev Player): Pass\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Landlord (Opponent)]: 13\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Peasant (Teammate)]: 3\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nRedJoker: 1, K: 1, Q: 1, J: 1, 10: 1, 9: 1, 8: 2, 7: 1, 6: 2, 5: 2, 4: 2, 3: 1\nValid Moves:\nsingle: ♥2\nsingle: BlackJoker\npass: []\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Evaluation: Beating ♠A requires a higher single. Options are ♥2 or BlackJoker, or pass. Using BlackJoker is very costly (it’s near-absolute control and can enable a rocket if you later get/need red joker), while ♥2 is a strong but more expendable stopper. Teammate has only 3 cards; preserving maximum control to respond to landlord’s endgame is important, so spending the 2 now is preferable to spending the joker.\nReason: Play ♥2 to win the trick without wasting BlackJoker, keeping the joker for later to block a critical landlord play or to secure control when teammate is about to go out.\nAnswer: {"cards":["♥2"]}'}
